\pard\tx2380\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380\fc0\cf0 DESCRIPTION	
\b SNDAcquire()
\b0  attempts to gain ownership of the sound resources specified in 
\i soundResource
\i0 , a value that's created by (bitwise) or'ing a combination of the following resource codes:\

\fs20 \

\fs4 \

\pard\tx6420\tx10440\f2\b\fs28\li2760\fc0\cf0 Code	Resource\

\fs6 \

\f0\b0\fs28 SND_ACCESS_OUT	sound-out \
SND_ACCESS_IN	sound-in\
SND_ACCESS_DSP	the DSP \

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 Alternatively, you can acquire the sound driver device port without gaining ownership of the device by passing 0 as the value of 
\i soundResource
\i0 .  \

\fs20 \

\fs28 Device and ownership ports to a successfully acquired sound resource are returned in 
\i devicePort
\i0  and 
\i ownerPort
\i0 , respectively.  If you pass a previously created port as the value of 
\i devicePort
\i0 , that port is used; passing a value of PORT_NULL (0) causes 
\b SNDAcquire()
\b0  to create a port for you.  The value you pass through 
\i ownerPort
\i0  is ignored by the function; a new owner port is always created.   \

\fs20 \

\fs28 Acquiring a resource makes it active, such that other acquisition requests may fail, even if the requests are in the same process.  You can grant a priority to the acquisition by setting the value of the 
\i priority
\i0  argumentÐin a subsequent call to 
\b SNDAcquire()
\b0 , the acquisition with the higher priority wins.  The 
\i preempt
\i0  flag is used as a tie-breaker.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 The function's 
\i timeout
\i0 , 
\i negFun
\i0 , and 
\i arg
\i0  arguments are currently unused.  \

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 The ports that are created and returned by SNDAcquire()
\b0  can be passed as arguments to certain sound driver functions (functions that are prefixed ªsnddriverº).  Furthermore, there's not much reason to call 
\b SNDAcquire()
\b0  unless this is what you're doing:  Although you can use the function generally to query for the existence of a particular resource, there's not much point in acquiring a sound device if all you're going to do is call other 
\b SND...() 
\b0 functions.\

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 SNDReset()
\b0  and 
\b SNDRelease()
\b0  reset to a virgin state and release, respectively, the specified resources.  The resources must have been previously acquired through 
\b SNDAcquire()
\b0 ; the device and owner port arguments are values returned by that function.  
\b SNDRelease()
\b0  sets the owner port to PORT_NULL; the device port is unaffected.\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	If no error occurs, SND_ERR_NONE is returned.  Otherwise, an error code, as described in 
\b SNDSoundError()
\b0 , is returned.  \

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\fs28\fi-1360 ERRORS	If 
\b SNDAcquire()
\b0  is unable to acquire any one of the resources specified in 
\i soundResource
\i0 , none of the resources are acquired.  \

