\pard\tx2380\f0\b0\fs28\fi-1560\li2380\fc0\cf0 SUMMARY	Create and free a sound structure \

\fs30 \

\fs28\fi-1960 DECLARED IN	sound/utilsound.h\

\fs30 \

\fs28\fi-1940\li2760 SYNOPSIS	int 
\b SNDAlloc(
\b0 SNDSoundStruct **
\i sound
\i0 , int 
\i dataSize
\i0 , int 
\i dataFormat
\i0 , int€
\i samplingRate
\i0 , int 
\i channelCount
\i0 , int 
\i infoSize
\b\i0 )\

\pard\b0\fi-380\li2760\fc0\cf0 int 
\b SNDFree(
\b0 SNDSoundStruct *
\i sound
\b\i0 )\

\fs30 \

\pard\tx2380\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380\fc0\cf0 DESCRIPTION	The SNDSoundStruct structure is the data format used by the sound software to encapsulate a sound.  It defines the soundfile format and the sound pasteboard type, and it lies at the heart of every Sound object.  
\b SNDAlloc()
\b0  creates and returns, in 
\i sound
\i0 , a new SNDSoundStruct.  The arguments to 
\b SNDAlloc()
\b0  correspond to the SNDSoundStruct fields described below.  
\b SNDFree()
\b0  frees the SNDSoundStruct pointed to by 
\i sound.
\i0   You should always use 
\b SNDFree()
\b0  to free a sound structure created through 
\b SNDAlloc()
\b0 .  \

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 The fields of the SNDSoundStruct structure list the attributes of the sound that the structure represents.  The sound data itself isn't contained in the structure, but is located by a structure field.  Nonetheless, it's often convenient to think of a SNDSoundStruct as containing the sound data that it represents.  By convention, the structure is referred to as the sound's ªheader.º  It's defined as:\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx3140\tx3900\tx4400\tx4900\tx5400\tx5920\tx6420\tx6920\tx7420\tx7920\tx8440\tx8940\tx9440\tx9940\tx10440\tx10960\f4\fs24\li2760\fc0\cf0 typedef struct  \{\
    int  magic;         /* SND_MAGIC ((int)0x2e736e64) */\
    int  dataLocation;  /* Offset or pointer to the raw data */\
    int  dataSize;      /* Raw data size in bytes */\
    int  dataFormat;    /* The data format code */\
    int  samplingRate;  /* The sampling rate */\
    int  channelCount;  /* The number of channels */\
    char info[4];       /* Textual information about the sound */\
SNDSoundStruct;\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\f0\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 The 
\b magic
\b0  field is a magic number that identifies a SNDSoundStruct.  It's automatically set when you allocate the structure.  \

\fs20 \

\fs28 The 
\b dataLocation
\b0  field indicates the location of the actual sound data.  Usually, the data immediately follows the header.  In this case, 
\b dataLocation
\b0  is the offset from the beginning of the structure to the first byte of the sound dataÐin other words, it's the size of the sound's header.  However, if you edit the sound through functions such as 
\b SNDDeleteSamples()
\b0  or 
\b SNDInsertSamples()
\b0 , the sound can become fragmented such that the data no longer follows the header.  In this case, 
\b dataLocation
\b0  is a pointer to a NULL-terminated block of addresses, each of which points to a separate SNDSoundStruct.  The collection of these SNDSoundStructs make up the fragmented data.  \

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 dataSize
\b0  is the size, in bytes, of the memory allocated for the sound data.  The memory is initialized to zero.  \

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 dataFormat
\b0  describes the sound data as one of the following codes:\

\fs20 \

\fs4 \

\pard\tx7200\tx10440\f2\b\fs28\li2760\fc0\cf0 Code
\b0 	
\b Format
\b0  \

\pard\tx6420\tx10440\fs6\li2760\fc0\cf0 \

\pard\tx7200\tx10440\f0\fs28\li2760\fc0\cf0 SND_FORMAT_MULAW_8	8-bit mu-law samples\
SND_FORMAT_LINEAR_8	8-bit linear samples\
SND_FORMAT_LINEAR_16	16-bit linear samples\
SND_FORMAT_EMPHASIZED	16-bit linear with emphasis\
SND_FORMAT_COMPRESSED	16-bit linear with compression\
SND_FORMAT_COMPRESSED_EMPHASIZED	A combination of the two above\
SND_FORMAT_LINEAR_24	24-bit linear samples\
SND_FORMAT_LINEAR_32	32-bit linear samples\
SND_FORMAT_FLOAT	floating-point samples\
SND_FORMAT_DOUBLE	double-precision float samples\
SND_FORMAT_DSP_DATA_8	8-bit fixed-point samples\
SND_FORMAT_DSP_DATA_16	16-bit fixed-point samples\
SND_FORMAT_DSP_DATA_24	24-bit fixed-point samples\
SND_FORMAT_DSP_DATA_32	32-bit fixed-point samples\
SND_FORMAT_DSP_CORE	DSP program\
SND_FORMAT_DISPLAY	non-audio display data\
SND_FORMAT_INDIRECT	fragmented sampled data\
SND_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED	unspecified format \

\pard\tx6420\tx10440\fs20\li2760\fc0\cf0 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 All but the last five formats identify different sizes and types of sampled data.  The others deserve special note:  \

\fs20 \

\fs28\fi-380\li2760 ·	SND_FORMAT_DSP_CORE format contains data that represents a loadable DSP core program.  Sounds in this format are required by the 
\b SNDBootDSP()
\b0  and 
\b SNDRunDSP()
\b0  functions.  You create a SND_FORMAT_DSP_CORE sound by reading a DSP load file (extension ª.lodº) with the 
\b SNDReadDSPfile()
\b0  function.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 ·	SND_FORMAT_DISPLAY format is used by the Sound Kit's SoundView class.  Such sounds can't be played.  \

\fs20 \

\fs28 ·	SND_FORMAT_INDIRECT indicates data that has become fragmented due to editing.€€Only sampled data can become fragmented.  You never allocate a sound with this format.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 ·	SND_FORMAT_UNSPECIFIED is used for unrecognized formats.\

\fs20 \

\b\fs28\fi0\li2380 samplingRate
\b0  is also given as a code and should be cast into an 
\b int
\b0 .  The NeXT sound hardware supports the following sampling rates for recording and playback:\

\fs20 \

\fs4 \

\pard\tx6420\tx10440\f2\b\fs28\li2760\fc0\cf0 Code
\b0 	
\b Sampling Rate (Hz)\

\fs6 \

\f0\b0\fs28 SND_RATE_CODEC	8012.8210513\
SND_RATE_LOW	22050\
SND_RATE_HIGH	44100\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\b\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 channelCount
\b0  is the number of channels of sound.  Playback of one- and two-channel sounds is supported; a sound with more than two channels is unplayable.  \

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 infoSize
\b0  is the size of a variable-length string that can be used to textually describe the sound.  The size is extended to the next 4-byte boundary (the minimum size is 4 bytes).  You can't increase the length of the info string once its size has been set.  \

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	If no error occurs, SND_ERR_NONE is returned.  Otherwise, an error code, as described in 
\b SNDSoundError()
\b0 , is returned.  \

\fs20 \

