\pard\f2\b\fs28\fi-760\li3140\fc0\cf0 SNDCompressSound()\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\f0\b0\fs28\fi-1560\li2380\fc0\cf0 SUMMARY	Compress or decompress a sound\

\fs30 \

\fs28\fi-1960 DECLARED IN	sound/convertsound.h\

\fs30 \

\fs28\fi-1940\li2760 SYNOPSIS	int 
\b SNDCompressSound(
\b0 SNDSoundStruct *
\i fromSound
\i0 , SNDSoundStruct€**
\i toSound
\i0 , BOOL 
\i bitFaithful
\i0 , int€
\i compressionAmount
\b\i0 )\

\fs30 \

\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380 DESCRIPTION	
\b SNDCompressSound()
\b0  creates and returns, in 
\i toSound
\i0 , a new SNDSoundStruct that contains a compressed or decompressed version of the sound in 
\i fromSound
\i0 :\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\fi-380\li2760\fc0\cf0 ·	If 
\i fromSound's
\i0  format is SND_FORMAT_LINEAR_16 or SND_FORMAT_EMPHASIZED, the sound returned in 
\i toSound
\i0  is compressed.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 ·	If its format is SND_FORMAT_COMPRESSED or SND_FORMAT_COMPRESSED_EMPHASIZED, the sound is decompressed.\

\fs20 \

\fs28\fi0\li2380 No other formats are allowed; in addition, the sound can't have more than two channels.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 The function's 
\i bitFaithful
\i0  and 
\i compressionAmount
\i0  arguments are used only when compressing:\

\fs20 \

\fs28\fi-380\li2760 ·	
\i bitFaithful
\i0  determines the fidelity with which a compressed sound can be restored to its original state.  If 
\i bitFaithful
\i0  is YES, the sound returned in 
\i toSound
\i0  can be decompressed to exactly match the original sound data; if it's NO, some degradation can be expected.  \

\fs20 \

\fs28 ·	The 
\i compressionAmount
\i0  argument controls the amount of compression.  Its value ranges from 4 to 8 with higher numbers giving more compression but less fidelity.  Depending on the signal, a 
\i compressionAmount
\i0  of 4 will compress the sound to about half its original size; a value of 8 compresses to about one-sixth the size.  For bit-faithful compression, you should set 
\i compressionAmount
\i0  to 4.\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	If no error occurs, SND_ERR_NONE is returned.  Otherwise an error code, as described in 
\b SNDSoundError()
\b0 , is returned.\

\fs20 \

