\pard\tx2380\f0\b0\fs28\fi-1560\li2380\fc0\cf0 SUMMARY	Convert between logarithmic and linear units\

\fs30 \

\fs28\fi-1960 DECLARED IN	SoundKit/NXSoundDevice.h\

\fs30 \

\fs28\fi-1940\li2760 SYNOPSIS	float 
\b SNDConvertDecibelsToLinear(
\b0 float 
\i dB
\b\i0 )\

\pard\b0\fi-380\li2760\fc0\cf0 float 
\b SNDConvertLinearToDecibels(
\b0 float 
\i linear
\b\i0 )\

\fs30 \

\pard\tx2380\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380\fc0\cf0 DESCRIPTION	These convenience functions convert from units of decibels to a linear value, and vice versa.  Decibels express the difference between two quantities in logarithmic units, while on a linear scale the same relationship is expressed as the ratio of the two quantities.  For example, a difference of zero decibels is equivalent to a ratio of 1.0.  The functions are, in their entirety:\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx3140\tx3900\tx4400\tx4900\tx5400\tx5920\tx6420\tx6920\tx7420\tx7920\tx8440\tx8940\tx9440\tx9940\tx10440\tx10960\f4\fs24\li2760\fc0\cf0 float SNDConvertDecibelsToLinear(float dB)\
\{\
    return (float)pow(10.0, (double)dB/20.0);\
\}\
\
float SNDConvertLinearToDecibels(float linear)\
\{\
    return (float)(20.0 * log10((double)linear));\
\}\

\fs80 \

