\pard\tx2380\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380\fc0\cf0 DESCRIPTION	
\b SNDConvertSound()
\b0  copies the sampled data from 
\i fromSound
\i0  into 
\i toSound
\i0 , converting the copied data to the format, channel count, and sampling rate specified by 
\i toSound
\i0 .  Memory for the converted data is automatically allocated.  The following conversions are possible:\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\fi-380\li2760\fc0\cf0 ·	Arbitrary sampling rate conversion.\
·	Compression and decompression.\
·	Floating-point formats (including double-precision) to and from linear formats.\
·	Mono to stereo.\
·	CODEC mu-law to and from linear formats.\

\fs20 \

\b\fs28\fi0\li2380 SNDMulaw()
\b0  converts a value from 16-bit linear to mu-law:  It takes a single linear 16-bit argument and returns the corresponding mu-law value.  
\b SNDiMulaw()
\b0  performs the inverse operation:  It takes a mu-law argument and returns the 16-bit linear value.\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	If no error occurs, 
\b SNDConvertSound()
\b0  returns SND_ERR_NONE.  Otherwise an error code, as described in 
\b SNDSoundError()
\b0 , is returned.\

\fs20 \

