\fs30 \

\pard\tx2380\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380\fc0\cf0 DESCRIPTION	
\b SNDGetNumberOfATCBands()
\b0  returns, by reference in 
\i numBands
\i0 , the number of frequency bands that 
\b SNDCompressSound()
\b0  uses for compressing sounds with ATC (Audio Transform Compression).   Currently, this number is always 40.\

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\b\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 SNDGetATCBandFrequencies()
\b0  fills the array 
\i centerFreqs
\i0  with floating-point numbers that specify the center frequency in Hertz of each band.  Similarly, the array filled by 
\b SNDGetATCBandwidths()
\b0  contains the width in Hertz of each band.  The first argument to each of these functions should be the value returned by 
\b SNDGetNumberOfATCBands()
\b0 .\

\fs20 \

\fs28 The ATC bands correspond roughly to the ªcritical bandsº of hearing.  Band zero is centered at zero Hz, and the highest band is centered at half the sampling rate.  The bandwidths and spacing are uniform below a certain frequency, above which the bands are progressively wider in Hertz and spaced further apart.  For sounds having the standard sampling rate of 44.1 kHz, bands below 1000 Hz have the same bandwidth, while bands above 1000 Hz have bandwidths of approximately 20% of the band's center frequency.  For sounds with other sampling rates, the bands' frequencies are scaled so that the same number of bands covers zero Hz to half the sampling rate, whatever the latter may be.  
\b SNDGetATCBandFrequencies()
\b0  and 
\b SNDGetATCBandwidths()
\b0  assume a 44.1-kHz sampling rate when filling the arrays 
\i centerFreqs
\i0  and 
\i bandwidths
\i0 , respectively.  To obtain the correct values for other sampling rates, multiply each element of the returned arrays by the ratio of the sampling rate to 44.1 kHz.\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	0 is returned unless the host isn't a NeXT computer, in which case ATC is unavailable.\

