\pard\tx2380\b0\fs28\fi-1960\li2380\fc0\cf0 DESCRIPTION	
\b SNDReserve()
\b0  attempts to gain ownership of the sound resources specified in 
\b\i soundResource
\b0\i0 , a value that's created by (bitwise) or'ing a combination of the following resource codes:\

\fs20 \

\fs4 \

\pard\tx6420\tx10440\f2\b\fs28\li2760\fc0\cf0 Code	Resource\

\fs6 \

\f0\b0\fs28 SND_ACCESS_OUT	sound out\
SND_ACCESS_IN	sound in\
SND_ACCESS_DSP	the DSP \

\fs20 \

\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 The 
\i priority
\i0  argument is used, ostensibly, to determine whether a particular reservation can supercede an existing one.  However, the priority scheme doesn't work between applicationsÐif you successfully reserve a sound resource, no other application can take it from you, regardless of the relative priority values that were used in the respective 
\b SNDReserve()
\b0  calls.  (The priority argument does have an affect within the same application, but there really isn't much reason for one part of an application to steal sound resources from another part.)\

\fs20 \

\fs28 Despite this, 
\b SNDReserve()
\b0  isn't utterly useless; it eliminates some of the overhead of acquiring and setting up a device that would otherwise occur upon each instance of playback (or recording).  For example, if you want to play a series of soundfiles, you stand a better chance of seamless playback if you first reserve the sound-out device.\

\fs20 \

\fs28 Use of 
\b SNDReserve()
\b0  is optional; prioritized access to the appropriate resource is established when either the 
\b SNDStartPlaying()
\b0  or the 
\b SNDStartRecording()
\b0  function is called.  The process should eventually free its reserved resources by calling 
\b SNDUnreserve()
\b0 .  Sound resources are automatically freed when the process terminates.\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\pard\tx2380\fs28\fi-1320\li2380\fc0\cf0 RETURN	If no error occurs, SND_ERR_NONE is returned.  Otherwise, an error code, as described in 
\b SNDSoundError()
\b0 , is returned.\

\fs20 \

\fs10 \

\fs28\fi-1360 ERRORS	If 
\b SNDReserve()
\b0  is unable to reserve any one of the resources specified in 
\i soundResource
\i0 , it won't reserve any of them.\

\fs20 \

