\pard\tx2760\tx3140\tx3520\fs28\li2380\fc0\cf0 SNDWriteSoundfile()
\b0  writes the specified sound structure as the soundfile.  
\i path
\i0  is a full pathname that should include the ª.sndº extension (the convention for soundfiles).  The function automatically opens and closes the file.\

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 SNDWrite()
\b0  also writes a complete soundfile, but its argument is a file descriptor rather than a pathname.  The file must be open for writing.  \

\fs20 \

\fs28 With both 
\b SNDWriteSoundfile()
\b0  and 
\b SNDWrite()
\b0 , the actual sound data is written as a contiguous block, even if 
\i sound
\i0  is fragmented.  However, 
\i sound
\i0  itself isn't affectedÐif it's fragmented, it remains fragmented.  \

\fs20 \

\b\fs28 SNDWriteHeader()
\b0  is similar to 
\b SNDWrite()
\b0 , but it only writes 
\i sound
\i0 's header to the file.  \

